Chapter: Sha512

 SHA-512 cryptographic hash function producing a 512-bit (8-word) digest
 from an arbitrary-length byte list. The algorithm operates on 64-bit
 words, pads input to a multiple of 1024 bits, expands each 16-word
 block into an 80-word message schedule, and compresses through 80
 rounds of mixing.

 A Sha512State is a record containing:
 a, b, c, d, e, f, g, h -- eight 64-bit working variables.

 To sha512 gives List Integer,
 hashing a byte list and returning eight 64-bit words as the digest.

 To sha512-to-hex gives Text,
 formatting an 8-word digest as a 128-character lowercase hex string.

 To sha512-text-to-bytes gives List Integer,
 converting a text string to a list of byte values.

 We say:

Section: 64-bit Word Helpers

  k64 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  k64 (hi) (lo) = bit-or (bit-shl hi 32) lo

  mask64-lo : Integer = k64 0 4294967295

  w64-add : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  w64-add (a) (b) = bit-and (a + b) (k64 4294967295 4294967295)

  rotr64 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rotr64 (x) (n) =
    bit-or (bit-shru x n) (bit-shl x (64 - n))

Section: SHA-512 Functions

  sha512-sigma0 : Integer -> Integer
  sha512-sigma0 (x) = bit-xor (rotr64 x 1) (bit-xor (rotr64 x 8) (bit-shru x 7))

  sha512-sigma1 : Integer -> Integer
  sha512-sigma1 (x) = bit-xor (rotr64 x 19) (bit-xor (rotr64 x 61) (bit-shru x 6))

  sha512-big-sigma0 : Integer -> Integer
  sha512-big-sigma0 (x) = bit-xor (rotr64 x 28) (bit-xor (rotr64 x 34) (rotr64 x 39))

  sha512-big-sigma1 : Integer -> Integer
  sha512-big-sigma1 (x) = bit-xor (rotr64 x 14) (bit-xor (rotr64 x 18) (rotr64 x 41))

  sha512-ch : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sha512-ch (x) (y) (z) = bit-xor (bit-and x y) (bit-and (bit-not x) z)

  sha512-maj : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sha512-maj (x) (y) (z) = bit-xor (bit-and x y) (bit-xor (bit-and x z) (bit-and y z))

